From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:23:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Four general space facts out of Machines/ARMWidth:
 logSpace_le_succ and logSpace_le_of_le_mul_two_pow to SpaceComplexity/Basic;
 LOGSPACE_subset_PSPACE and SPACE_succ_pow_subset_PSPACE to SpaceClasses;
 Constructible's two inline steps cite logSpace_le_succ

The ledger's LS-1 family, retired ahead of the dedup window so that the space hierarchy's fill can
cite these results from its imports. ARMWidth's edit is mechanical: the four declarations move,
unchanged in name and statement, and every user already imports the new homes; ARMWidth keeps the
register-machine wrappers. SpaceClasses imports ClassP/P (for succ_pow_le): one module, no new
Mathlib root, no simp lemma, and every module downstream of SpaceClasses already imports it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
